libcrypt-openssl-rsa-perl (0.35-1.1+veforge1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Re-enable PKCS#1 v1.5 padding for signatures (revert upstream's
    blanket croak; the Marvin attack only affects decryption).
  * Only pass explicitly-set, signature-valid padding modes to
    sign/verify and check the result. The previous ignored failure left
    "illegal or unsupported padding mode" on the OpenSSL error queue,
    which made pveproxy abort TLS connections during large uploads
    (ISO upload failure). Mirrors Proxmox's 0.35-1.1 rebuild.

 -- pxvirt <pxvirt@localhost>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 05:30:00 -0700

libcrypt-openssl-rsa-perl (0.35-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Team upload.
  * Set Homepage in debian/control to MetaCPAN page.
    Thanks to Matt Taggart for the bug report. (Closes: #1087888)
  * Import upstream version 0.35.
    - Disable PKCS#1 v1.5 padding. It's not practical to mitigate marvin
      attacks so we will instead disable this and require alternatives to
      address the issue.
      Resolves CVE-2024-2467.
    Closes: #1066969
  * Update debian/upstream/metadata.
  * Refresh Makefile.PL-no-ssl-in-LIBS.patch.
  * Declare compliance with Debian Policy 4.7.2.

